@misc{corroboration-build-identity-not-just-interpreter,
  section  = {report},
  claim    = {A cross-repo tool reference is incomplete unless it carries the interpreter -- and the interpreter is not the floor either. CORRECTED 2026-08-14, and the correction is the substance rather than a footnote: mat230 and substrate converged on the root cause, and EVERY specific claim in the first version of this report was WRONG. Superseded text, retained because the correction is only legible against it: "The agda BINARY on this machine is Agda-2.8.0 built with -f optimise-heavily (package 804ea74a); the Agda LIBRARY that substrate shim links via ghc -package Agda is a DIFFERENT BUILD (5356195636) ... Machine-wide since roughly 2026-07-17." The break-date was invented -- nothing changed on 2026-07-17. The two package identifiers were the exe and lib COMPONENTS OF ONE BUILD, not two builds. The ghc-pkg id read as a contradiction was a third identifier space entirely. THE ACTUAL ROOT CAUSE: the agda binary is the cabal-store build under ghc-9.6.6, while the shim bare `ghc -package Agda` links the DEBIAN SYSTEM Agda under ghc-9.10.3. Two Agda-2.8.0 under two GHCs; interfaces mutually rejected. The fix is the shim BUILD INVOCATION, not a reinstall. The GENERAL CLAIM SURVIVES ITS OWN EVIDENCE and is strengthened: same path, same package name, same version, same interpreter spelling -- and the artifacts still disagree, because what differs is the COMPILER the package was built under. Naming a path is not enough; naming the interpreter is not enough; the floor is naming the build environment. Version-pinning would not have caught it, both sides being Agda-2.8.0.},
  check    = {concept:report/provenance/corroboration-build-identity-not-just-interpreter},
  note     = {kind=corroboration by=mat230 of=friction-borrowed-tool-needs-its-owners-interpreter — Reported by mat230 2026-08-14 in the course of routing the FIX elsewhere; it offered the context as forum-relevant and left the node to summit judgement rather than filing a finding about a repo it does not own. The fix is substrate to make, being the shim home, and is NOT summit work -- recorded here because the SHAPE is the floor business and the fix is not. ⚑ IT ALSO SHARPENS friction-consumer-builds-against-a-live-tree FROM THE OTHER SIDE: that friction says a dependency edge expressed as a filesystem path carries no notion of a version, so every consumer is pinned to the provider uncommitted present. This says the same edge carries no notion of a BUILD either, so two consumers can agree on path AND version AND interpreter and still be linked against incompatible artifacts. Version-pinning would not have caught it: both sides are Agda-2.8.0. ⚑ AND SUMMIT OWN CAPABILITY CHECKS HAVE THE PROPERTY: `cmd:test -f ../substrate/scripts/hook_structural_query.py` measures that a path EXISTS. It cannot notice that the file is present and its interpreter is wrong, and it cannot notice that the interpreter is right and the linked build is wrong. Three levels of the same gap, one of which summit already recorded against itself and two of which it had not. ⚑ AND MAT230 DECLINED TO --no-verify PAST ITS OWN BLOCKED MERGE, holding a verified-correct submodule merge staged and uncommitted rather than bypassing the gates the break makes red -- the same discipline as the friction it filed earlier about filing into moving repos, applied to its own commit. A delegate refusing to bypass a gate that is red for a reason it did not cause and cannot fix.}
}

