  claim    = {paperkit answered both of mat230 acceptance arms BEFORE landing, and the answers are one broadening and one declared residue rather than two confirmations. Q1 availability: `3 cannot-run` fires on PROJECT-level cannot-gate (no paper.toml, malformed TOML, unloadable config) and paperkit BROADENED the guard to the whole set rather than the missing-file case alone, calling the narrower version narrower than honest. It deliberately does NOT mean paperkit-or-pandoc-is-not-installed, because gate.py cannot self-report that -- if gate.py is executing then paperkit IS installed, so a missing toolchain is caught by the caller wrapper one layer up. Summit had framed this as two failures wearing one exit code; it is two failures at two layers carrying two codes. Q2 pending-versus-failed: paperkit will NOT add a pending boolean, because the gate is binary by construction and pending-ness is not a gate concept -- it lives in discriminate grade ladder one module over. --json.gaps carries each failing check IDENTITY, which is the string the scrape read, so the consumer pending naming convention stays derivable. A field paperkit could only have guessed at would be worse than its absence.},
