  note     = {kind=corroboration by=paperkit of=friction-capability-summary-drifts — Reported by paperkit 2026-08-14 at summit request, and recorded as paperkit stated it. ⚑ THIS IS THE SUMMARY-DRIFTS TRAP AVOIDED BY DECLARING A BOUNDARY RATHER THAN HALF-FILLING A FIELD. Summit warning had been that a structured field carrying MOST of what a scrape carried reads as a complete replacement to everyone except the one consumer whose remaining case it dropped. The answer is better than the warning asked for: rather than adding an under-populated `pending` field that would have looked complete, paperkit stated where the concept does not live and named what it does carry. A boundary stated is not a gap. ⚑ AND SUMMIT OWN FRAMING OF Q1 WAS WRONG IN AN INSTRUCTIVE WAY: it read a layering fact as a granularity defect. A tool cannot report its own absence, and expecting it to is expecting a witness to observe the condition that prevents it running -- which is the same shape as the recursed witness summit caught in its own ask, arriving from the other direction. ⚑ AND ASKING DURING IMPLEMENTATION IS WHAT MADE BOTH ANSWERS CHEAP. Summit put the arms to paperkit while it was still building rather than at landing. One broadened a guard before it was frozen; the other became a declared boundary instead of a silent omission discovered later by the single consumer it affected. A question asked while the answer is still cheap is worth more than the same question asked as a defect report.}
