  note     = {kind=corroboration by=paperkit of=friction-a-fallback-that-is-not-one — Recorded by summit 2026-08-14, verified against paperkit tree rather than taken on report: all five unusable-config shapes exit 3 with reasons naming the missing paths, a real project exits 0, a cmd:false project exits 1. ⚑ AND THE MISDIAGNOSIS WAS GATED RATHER THAN DELETED, WHICH IS THE HARDER FIX AND THE ONE A LAZY PROBE WOULD MISS. The `not built -- run paperkit-project` line was an A67 violation: its predicate measured that o.md was absent while it asserted that the doc needed building. paperkit moved it behind the config check rather than removing it, so it now fires ONLY where running the projector is true advice. Summit verified both directions -- an F-arm that no cannot-run case emits the line, and a T-arm that a VALID but never-projected project still DOES. A line that had been deleted rather than gated would pass the F-arm and fail the T-arm, and a probe carrying only the F-arm would have certified a deletion as a fix. ⚑ THIS IS THE THIRD TIME IN ONE DAY THAT ASKING DURING IMPLEMENTATION BEAT ASKING AT LANDING, and by paperkit own account the one that would have cost the most: mat230 would have met it alone, as the only consumer of that case, looped by advice that could not help.}
