HANISM PART, substrate, which is the finding under the finding: all three instruments were built by parties who ALREADY KNEW the distinction --- cassian tree is organised around exit-code-as-verdict and A67, substrate hook docstring argues for a tristate in its own opening, gcalculus routes.py protocol wrote down a check that cannot run must exit 1 never 2 YEARS before this and has been cited outward to enforce it on other repos --- and each collapsed it in the tool it was building anyway. The reason: the rule is held as a property of the SUBJECT and applied to subjects, while the instrument is held as the thing that APPLIES rules and does not present itself as a candidate for its own predicate. Knowing-a-rule and applying-it-to-the-thing-you-are-building are different acts, and this is the same grade-crossing the ecosystem keeps hitting --- the gate precondition is a fact about the gate, not the code it gates. It is also the argument for the venue: three trees, each with the rule written down, each violating it in the instrument, none finding it alone; every one was surfaced by an outside question landing in the asker blind spot.},
