which is the buildable part: its workaround-refuse-the-empty-population says report n of m and refuse an empty population, and STATE THE POPULATION IN THE VERDICT LINE IS NOT ENOUGH WHEN THE PROXY IS VALID OVER A SUBSET --- zero point five was a true statement about a population of TEN that governs a population of TWO. The fuller form is STATE THE POPULATION THE PREDICATE IS VALID OVER, NOT THE POPULATION IT WAS COMPUTED OVER, and those differ exactly when a proxy drops a variable. ⚑ FINALLY, NO GATE COULD HAVE CAUGHT IT BECAUSE THE GATE WOULD HAVE BEEN THE WRONG RELATION: what caught it was stating the constraint declaratively and then measuring the geometry it claimed to describe, which is the same move as reading the m in n of m applied to a relation instead of a count},
