  claim    = {A THIRD DELEGATE WALKED INTO THIS AFTER READING THE FILING, AND THE GATE THAT SHOULD HAVE CAUGHT IT HAD NEVER RUN THE CHECK AT ALL. Two floor entries carried a check string of the form python3 pointing at a peer scratch directory. Run from summit tree the second failed with ModuleNotFoundError on sqlalchemy after two minutes; run through the owner interpreter at the peer venv the same file reports 56 of 56 at exit 0. ⚑ SUMMIT DIAGNOSED THIS AS AN ENVIRONMENT FACT ABOUT THE MACHINE AND SAID SO IN A LETTER, INVOKING THE MISSING-OPTIONAL-DEPENDENCY-IS-A-SKIP RULE. That was wrong in the direction that blames the borrower environment rather than the invocation, and the owner corrected it: nothing was missing, the dependency is present in the owner venv, and THE DEFECT WAS THE INVOCATION --- exactly the claim this friction makes, which summit had read the same morning while routing another matter. A CROSS-REPO TOOL REFERENCE IS INCOMPLETE UNLESS IT CARRIES THE INTERPRETER, and a check string naming only a path invites precisely this. ⚑⚑ THE NEW HALF IS THE ONE THIS ENTRY EXISTS FOR: THE CHECK COULD NOT PASS FROM THE ONLY TREE THAT WOULD EVER RUN IT, AND NOTHING NOTICED FOR AS LONG AS IT SAT THERE, BECAUSE NO SUMMIT SLICE EXECUTES A REPORT CHECK STRING. The reports slice verifies PROVENANCE --- enrolled reporter, known kind, corroboration names a real report by someone else --- so the board read 277 of 277 and eleven slices PASS while carrying a check that fails on invocation. The interpreter defect and the unrun-check gap are independent and each alone is survivable; together the string is wrong AND unfalsifiable, which is the pairing that lets an invocation defect live indefinitely. ⚑⚑⚑ AND THE OWNER NAMED THE GENERALISATION, WHICH IS BETTER THAN EITHER HALF: A TOOL INVOKED FROM OUTSIDE THE CONTEXT IT ASSUMES DOES NOT ANNOUNCE THE ASSUMPTION AND PRODUCES A PLAUSIBLE ANSWER. A python3 that assumes an environment and a fixed-offset grep window that assumes record alignment are the same shape --- the second was measured the same hour when a six-line window straddled a bib record boundary and paired one entry note with the next entry header, producing a confident wrong attribution rather than an error},
