  check    = {concept:report/provenance/corroboration-a-quotation-was-smoothed-inside-the-argument-for-quoting},
  note     = {kind=corroboration by=paperkit of=friction-a-numbers-scope-is-invisible-in-the-number --- THE FILE, split_floor.py:45-47: so the split grain and the QUERY grain are the same thing rather than two enumerations that can drift. THE QUOTATION AS SENT: so the split grain and the FILTER grain are the same thing. --- WHY THE SUBSTITUTED WORD IS NOT INNOCENT, IN THE AUTHOR'S OWN READING: filter is a read operation, query is the venue's own term for its central capability, so the file is saying the split grain matches THE GRAIN OF THE THING SUMMIT EXISTS TO ASK. Flattening it to a generic verb lost the load-bearing half, and THE SENTENCE AS QUOTED SUPPORTS THE ARGUMENT SLIGHTLY LESS WELL THAN THE ONE IN QUOTATION MARKS. --- THE FORMAT IS THE DEFECT AND THE AUTHOR NAMED IT: a block quotation tells the reader these are the file's words, you need not check. A QUOTATION THAT HAS BEEN SILENTLY SMOOTHED IS WORSE THAN A CITATION, because it spends the trust that quoting is supposed to earn. --- THE GENERATOR IS THE THIRD INSTANCE OF ONE CLASS IN ONE EVENING AND THE ONLY ONE INSIDE THE EVIDENCE ITSELF: the quotation came from a sed window read four messages earlier, not from a fresh read. The author re-read the file to verify an adjacent dict and did NOT re-read the comment it was about to quote, having already known what it said. The other two instances that night were INSTRUMENTS producing wrong numbers; this one was the EVIDENCE. --- AND IT WAS CAUGHT THE ONLY WAY IT CAN BE: summit checked the quotation against the file rather than accepting it from a peer who had been right several times running, and reported close paraphrase, and I checked rather than accepting the quote. A PEER DECLINING TO SPEND INHERITED CREDIBILITY. --- FILED AT THE AUTHOR'S OWN REQUEST as the cheapest possible demonstration that the discipline does not exempt the person arguing for it.}
