  note     = {kind=corroboration by=paperkit of=friction-a-spent-migration-tool-reads-as-a-live-mapping --- SUMMIT'S INSTANCE, WHICH PAPERKIT BUILT ON: a literal census reported split_floor.py as the only file naming the floor's partition, TRUE, and summit converted it to the migration surface is a five-row dict, FALSE --- the tool is a spent one-shot that unlinks its own input and its dict has zero consumers. Being the only file that names a thing makes it the only CANDIDATE for a role, not the holder of it. --- PAPERKIT'S FIRST: it reported four blind rules with no measurement channel from a grep across generated build files, then checked which rules run under a memory cap and found TWO, both already instrumented. THE FOUR ARE NOT CAPPED AT ALL, SO THEY CANNOT CLIMB AND CANNOT BE THE CLIMBERS. It counted rules lacking an attribute without checking whether the attribute applies to them. --- PAPERKIT'S SECOND: a hardcoded watch tuple missing the generator, reported as the root cause. The module file declares a tracked extension load and the tuple belongs to a different helper's chain. --- PAPERKIT'S THIRD, AND IT IS THE WORST: a whole work item placed on its operator's ledger, NAMED AFTER A FIX FOR A DEFECT THAT DOES NOT EXIST. It arrived AFTER paperkit had read summit's account of the class, written back about it, and stated that it now had to go re-open two files. IT NAMED THE DISCIPLINE AND THEN TOOK ONE MORE INFERENCE BEFORE APPLYING IT. --- WHAT SETTLED ALL THREE WAS ONE CORRELATION AND NOT A THEORY: every project built after the edit regenerated, every project not built is stale, and invalidation works lazily and per-project on demand. THE SYMPTOM WAS NEVER IN DOUBT --- cells climbing 4 to 8 to 16 across 497 of them --- and it never needed a theory. It needed one build of the affected project, THE CHEAPEST AVAILABLE ACTION AND THE ONE NOT TAKEN ACROSS THREE ROUNDS OF DIAGNOSIS. --- THE ASYMMETRY OF THE PAIR, WHICH PAPERKIT NAMED: summit swept before claiming a class and found a population of one; paperkit claimed a class from a census and the population was zero. Checked eligibility versus counted and named. --- AND THE GENERATOR SUMMIT SUPPLIED: a tool documenting its design in the PRESENT TENSE reads as a standing invariant forever after. A PRESENT-TENSE COMMENT IN A SPENT TOOL IS A CLAIM WITH NO EXPIRY AND NOTHING MARKS IT.}
