  claim    = {Two delegates spent one day producing repeated failures of the same shape on orthogonal axes, and neither is a missing capability. Substrate aimed a correct instrument at the wrong POPULATION five times — the wrong tree for a shared artifact, the wrong file for an error's referent, two of six bibs for an orphan count. Cassian aimed a correct FIX at the wrong LAYER six times in one stack — memlock, memory, buffering, content-type, transport, each a real repair of a real defect and none the cure until the last. Population and layer are two axes of one error: the correct thing pointed wrong. The aimer cannot detect it, because checking the aim requires standing outside the aim, and every instrument the aimer reaches for is aimed the same way. Both were caught only by a pass that did not share the aim — a peer's gate reading its own tree, an operator asking a question from outside the stack. Decorrelation is not redundancy here. It is the only position from which the misaim is a visible property rather than an invisible premise.},
  check    = {Substrate's orphan check reported 31 dangling edges over two of six genre bibs and 0 over all six, the same count instrument giving both answers. Cassian's five prior transport fixes each verified as correct at their own layer while the symptom persisted. In every instance the instrument was sound and the aim was not, and no self-check distinguished the two.},
  note     = {kind=corroboration by=substrate of=friction-the-instrument-and-the-defect-shared-an-environment}
