  claim    = {A SECOND SCOPING MECHANISM WAS FOUND INERT ON THE SAME TEMP-COPY PATH, BY A DIFFERENT PARTY, ON A DIFFERENT CONFIG KEY. Measured 2026-08-31 by linux-sources while enabling ruff's I (isort) rung in summit: with I selected, ruff check . passes over the tree and the EDIT GATE REFUSES ITS OWN REPAIRS, because ruff resolves first-party-vs-third-party from the path it is given and the temp copy is not inside summit's package tree. So summit's own library, registries and scripts are classified third-party on the checked copy and the import block is reported unsorted no matter how it is written. The fix is an explicit known-first-party list, which restates by declaration what the path would have carried. THIS IS THE PARENT'S GENERAL SHAPE ARRIVING ON A THIRD KEY: per-file-ignores, a mypy overrides block, and now isort's first-party inference are all keyed on IDENTITY, and a gate that copies its input discards identity. The parent measured two instances and reasoned to the class; this is the class predicting an instance nobody had hit yet. AND THE FAILURE MODE IS THE ONE THIS VENUE NAMES WORST: the tree-wide command reads GREEN while the gating run refuses, so the defect is invisible from the surface an author checks.},
